// IEC CIM (CGMES 3.0): the graph model and sample data
//
// Generated by ../../cypher.py from model.json and sample.json. Edit those and regenerate, rather than this file.
//
// A small part of the grid model of Northgrid, a fictional transmission system operator, as merged from the CGMES
// equipment, topology, steady state hypothesis, state variables, short circuit and geographical location profiles. An
// 85 km 400 kV line runs from Brookfield power station, where a 650 MVA generator feeds the grid through a 21/400 kV
// step-up transformer, to Ashby substation, where a 400/220 kV autotransformer with an on-load tap changer supplies a
// 220 kV load. The data has the substations, voltage levels, busbars, breakers, terminals, connectivity and
// topological nodes, current limits on the line, and the power flow solution: bus voltages and the flows at each
// terminal.
//
// Run it against an empty database of Neo4j 5 or later, Enterprise Edition, for its node key and property existence
// constraints, e.g. with cypher-shell -f model.cypher. It merges every node and relationship, so it can be run again.

// The model: its constraints

